刀，猫着身子，朝野鸡的方向挪了几步，然后看好距离，算好手上的力度，将手中的菜刀扔了出去。随之传来了咯咯……的悲鸣声。萧遗墨惊讶的望去，只见那只肥大的野鸡脚已经被她抛出去的菜刀给切断了，此刻正斜躺在草丛间，悲鸣不止：“太残忍了你。”“唉，没办法，谁让它是动物呢。”苏小凡走了过去，将依然在垂死挣扎的野鸡捡起来，拔了一根杂草捆绑起来，放进了篮子里，又捡回菜刀，在草丛里擦干上面的血迹。“用一个小石子射过去不就好了。”萧遗墨翻翻白眼，恍然大悟，原来还可以这样，早知道昨天就用这招对付那只肥兔子了，怎么会忘记了呢。不过嘛从前太过依赖武功，如今自身武功尽失，不知道扔出去石子儿能不能打中动物呢，看来得找机会尝试尝试。“唔，我习惯用刀了，各种各样的刀都可以，但不是刀就不行。”苏小凡放好后，又继续采摘小蘑菇，心里乐翻了天，晚上可以给她们熬鸡汤了。“为什么？”萧遗墨不解，她刚刚那可是相当的厉害啊，无论是力度还是精准度，都是拿捏的刚刚好。苏小凡瘪瘪嘴：“这个嘛，我也不知道，以前我也试过的，除了刀就不行。”从前跟朋友去酒吧的时候，也玩过那种小小的飞镖，但是一次也没有射中过，无论如何也想不明白，究竟是问题出在哪里。“呵……”萧遗墨意味深长的看着她，黑眸中闪烁着好奇的光芒，这个女人似乎比外表看起来的，好玩多了。“好了，我们回去吧。”苏小凡站起身，看了看满满一篮子的战利品，有刚抓的还在咯咯低鸣的野鸡，有诸多的野蘑菇，心中别提多开心了。慢慢的，总会有办法改善目前的生活状况的。在苏小凡他们两人走后一两个时辰，苏家院子里，就来了一大群的人，皆是上门来讨债的。贾氏疑惑的看着众人，这些人平日里甚少来逼债的，为何今日会都来了呢？然而，当目光落在人群后面的那一堆人身上后，贾氏越加的疑惑了，他们昨日才来过，为何今日又来了？“大妹子，听说你家小凡去给村长家小孙子当童养媳了，村长说会给你们一笔银子，所以大伙儿今天过来，问问，看能不能先还大家一些。”贾氏看向说话的人，此人乃是住在村尾的苏虎，是一夫的堂兄，此人性子随和，从未上门来要过债：“对不起，各位了，娘一早便去镇子上了，一会儿回来如果还有剩下的话就先还给大家。”“好。”苏虎也不再多言，笑着问：“大妹纸快生了吧？”“嗯，应该就在最近。”贾氏抚上肚子，低头浅笑。苏小凡拎着篮子牵着萧遗墨的小手回来的时候，远远的就看到院子中站的一大群人，随即加快了脚步，奶奶不在家，如果娘被人欺负了可怎么办。“一有钱就去买东买西，看来是没打算还大家钱了吧。”李氏站在人群后，粗着嗓子吼。此声一出，院内的众人都纷纷看向贾氏，想要看她对此会有什么说法。“并非如此……”贾氏略为纠结，虽然二弟妹她们昨日做的有些过分，但是说来说去总归是一家人，将她们的所为说出去未免会遭人笑话。“说不出话来了吧，大家来评评理，我们好心把钱借给她们，她们这一有钱了就压根不想还钱了还。”孟氏佯装出一脸伤心的对着众人说。“芷烟，你倒是说句话呀。”苏虎的老婆余氏（余小荷）见众人在那两人的煽动下都变了脸色，有些担心，走上前挽上贾氏的胳膊。“二婶婶三婶婶，你们可真是贵人多忘事儿。”一道清冷的声音响起，众人纷纷看去。“小凡，身子可好些了？”余氏的妹妹余小西见苏小凡走来，笑着迎了过去。苏小凡对她甜甜一笑，此人该是苏小凡唯一的一位朋友，两人经常一同上山摘野菜什么的。“我们忘记什么了？”孟氏在看到苏小凡手中牵的小娃娃之后，脸色瞬间变了，那就是村长的小孙子吗？如此精致的娃娃，那些原本准备好的想要用来奚落苏小凡一番的话语，此刻是没办法说出口了。村长家不但有钱，这小孙子又生的如此好，即便是上门做童养媳也不吃亏啊。苏小凡走到贾氏身旁站定，将手中的篮子递给萧遗墨，柔声说：“小宝贝儿，帮姐姐拎进去。”", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/chongfuchengyin-nongjiatongyangxi/8.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Chapter 8 Visiting to collect debts. \"Okay, let's go.\" Su Xiaofan glanced at the place where he picked wild vegetables yesterday, and then continued to climb up. It was still early today, so if he went up to take a look, he might also find some wild mushrooms or something. After more than half an hour, the two of them reached the top of the mountain. There were overgrown weeds among the trees, and there were many tree stumps left. They must have been cut down, and on those stumps, there were mushrooms growing in twos and threes. \"Why doesn't anyone come here to pick wild mushrooms?\" Su Xiaofan squatted down and picked the wild mushrooms and put them into the basket. Looking around, there were mushrooms on the wooden piles. Although there were not many people in the village, there should be people picking them. After all, in my memory, the people here were not very rich. \"It is said that a few years ago, someone died after eating wild mushrooms on the mountain. Since then, few people have gone up the mountain to pick them.\" Xiao Yimo also came over to help, constantly throwing nearby wild mushrooms into her basket. \"So that's it...\" Su Xiaofan searched through the original memory and found that there was indeed such a thing, and it seemed to be quite serious. Many people died, but that was several years ago. Why would the little baby know about it? He was only born not long ago. Seeming to sense her doubts, Xiao Yimo turned his back to her and said, \"I heard it after coming here.\" \"Oh, what I said...\" Su Xiaofan smiled in relief, and out of the corner of his eye, he saw a pheasant not far away, and said in a low voice: \" Little baby, don't move yet, squat down.\" After saying that, he took out the kitchen knife he had brought with him, leaned forward and moved a few steps in the direction of the pheasant, then looked at the distance, calculated the strength of his hand, and threw the kitchen knife in his hand. Then there was a gurgling... wailing sound. Xiao Yimo looked in surprise and saw that the fat pheasant's legs had been cut off by the kitchen knife she threw, and it was lying in the grass, wailing: \"You are so cruel.\" \"Oh, there is no way, who let it be an animal.\" Su Xiaofan walked over, picked up the pheasant that was still struggling, pulled out a weed, tied it up, put it in the basket, picked up the kitchen knife, and wiped the blood on it in the grass. \"Just shoot it with a pebble.\" Xiao Yimo rolled his eyes and suddenly realized that it could still be like this. If he had known that he had used this trick to deal with the fat rabbit yesterday, how could he have forgotten it. However, I relied too much on martial arts in the past, but now I have lost all my martial arts. I wonder if throwing stones can hit animals. It seems that I have to find an opportunity to try. \"Well, I'm used to using knives. All kinds of knives are fine, but not a knife.\" After putting them away, Su Xiaofan continued to pick mushrooms. He was so happy that he could make chicken soup for them in the evening. \"Why?\" Xiao Yimo was puzzled. What she did just now was quite powerful. Whether it was strength or accuracy, she had it just right. Su Xiaofan pursed his lips: \"Well, I don't know about that. I've tried it before, but it doesn't work except for knives.\" When I went to a bar with my friends, I also played with those small darts, but I never hit it once. I couldn't figure out what the problem was. \"Ha...\" Xiao Yimo looked at her meaningfully, with curiosity shining in his dark eyes. This woman seemed to be much more interesting than she appeared. \"Okay, let's go back.\" Su Xiaofan stood up and looked at the basket full of trophies. There were freshly caught pheasants that were still clucking and crowing, and there were many wild mushrooms. He felt so happy. Slowly, there will always be ways to improve your current living situation. An hour or two after Su Xiaofan and the others left, a large group of people came to the Su family yard, all coming to collect debts. Jia looked at everyone in confusion. These people rarely came to collect debts on weekdays. Why did they all come today? However, when his eyes fell on the group of people at the back of the crowd, Jia became more and more confused. They had only been here yesterday, why were they here again today? \"Sister, I heard that your Xiaofan went to work as a child bride for the village chief's grandson. The village chief said he would give you a sum of money, so we all came here today to ask if we could pay some back to you first.\" Jia looked at the person who spoke. This person was Su Hu, who lived at the end of the village. He was Kazuo's cousin. He had an easy-going personality. He has never come to ask for debts: \"I'm sorry, everyone. Mom went to town early in the morning. If there is anything left when she comes back later, she will pay it back to everyone first.\" \"Okay.\" Su Hu said nothing more and asked with a smile, \"Is the eldest sister giving birth soon?\" \"Well, it should be soon.\" Jia touched her belly and lowered her head with a smile. When Su Xiaofan came back with a basket and Xiao Yimo's little hand, he saw a large group of people standing in the yard from a distance, and then he quickened his pace. Grandma was not at home. What if my mother was bullied? \"As soon as I have money, I go shopping. It seems I have no intention of repaying everyone's money.\" Ms. Li stood behind the crowd and shouted in a rough voice. As soon as this sound came out, everyone in the courtyard looked at Jia, wanting to see what she would say about this. \"That's not the case...\" Ms. Jia was a little confused. Although the second brother and sister did a bit too much yesterday, they are still a family after all. If they tell what they did, they will be laughed at. \"I'm speechless. Let's judge. We kindly lent them the money, but now that they have money, they don't want to pay it back at all.\" Meng said to everyone pretending to be sad. \"Zhiyan, please say something.\" Su Hu's wife Yu Shi (Yu Xiaohe) saw that everyone's expressions changed under the instigation of those two people. She was a little worried and stepped forward to take Jia Shi's arm. \"Second Aunt and Third Aunt, you are really noble and forgetful.\" A cold voice sounded, and everyone looked around. \"Xiaofan, are you feeling better?\" Yu's sister Yu Xiaoxi", "title_en": "Chapter 8"}